Consolidate 0009-0012 into a single SQL + add brand_name / company_website UI in Settings

Database:
- supabase/migrations/0009-0012_consolidated_single_file.sql merges
  migrations 0009, 0010, 0011, and the new 0012 backfill into ONE
  file the user can paste into the Supabase SQL editor once. Every
  block uses IF NOT EXISTS / CREATE OR REPLACE so it is safe to re-run.
- Block 4 (new 0012) backfills invoice_payment_methods rows for every
  existing invoice that has none yet (using the company's currently
  active gateways, intersected with client.allowed_gateways when set).
  This is what makes the per-invoice gateway picker actually drive
  /pay/[id] for invoices created before migration 0009 ran.

Code:
- app/(authed)/settings/payments/page.tsx: brand_name + company_website
  inputs added to the App Settings card.
- app/api/settings/payments/route.ts: GET returns both new fields;
  POST writes them. The /api/settings/payments endpoint is now the
  single source of truth for "what is our brand called and what is
  our website URL". lib/branding.ts reads these and falls back to
  companies.name / BRAND_NAME_FALLBACK when they're empty.

tsc --noEmit: 0 errors.
